    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d740">

                <pb facs="0711" n="699" xml:id="pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R.N.C./52: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>S.S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">“Rex” at Sea</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-20T22:00:00">February 20,
                            1940—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 20—9:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Duggan.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d740-f1"/> Referring to the request of the
                    Brazilian Government<anchor n="26" xml:id="d740-f2"/> for our views concerning
                    most recent violation of the neutrality zone I feel that we should inform Brazil
                    that we are prepared to join the other Republics immediately in joint protest;
                    that we should however further state that we believe the Neutrality Committee
                    should be requested to undertake at once the formulation of the draft replies to
                    be submitted to all of the Republics for their approval as joint responses to be
                    sent to the communication addressed to the President of Panama by the
                    belligerents refusing to accede to the terms of the declaration of Panama; and
                    that the Neutrality Committee should be further requested to expedite its
                    preferential consideration of the implementation of the declaration.</p>
                <p>I believe our reply while fully supporting Brazil should make it clear that in
                    our opinion reiterated protests without the implementation above indicated would
                    be sterile and ultimately stultifying.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d740-f1" n="25" xml:id="d740-f1-content">
                <p>Laurence Duggan, Chief of the Division of the American Republics.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d740-f2" n="26" xml:id="d740-f2-content">
                <p>See note from the Panamanian Secretary of Foreign Affairs and Communications,
                    February 16, <ref target="#pg695">p. 695</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
